0..68 Comment "// A body whose result is a function value may end in a bare lambda."
69..71 Comment "//"
72..145 Comment "// The `return` before such a lambda states nothing that the written type"
146..219 Comment "// lacks. The checker therefore reads the lambda as the box that the body"
220..283 Comment "// returns, and the core equals the core of a written `return`."
284..286 Comment "//"
287..360 Comment "// The lambda stands at the end of a body, after a `let`, at the end of a"
361..437 Comment "// block, and in each arm of a match. The cases with a written `return` keep"
438..516 Comment "// it under `explicit_exits`. Two cases keep their `return` in every source: a"
517..593 Comment "// box whose computation is no function, and a lambda with no expected type."
594..596 Comment "//"
597..612 Comment "// - see: #6390"
